{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And he continued yet further to speak to him.</b> The reason for his saying ״וַיּוֹסֶף״, and also for his saying the word ״אֵלָיו״: meaning, he added to pray within the first category itself — that the Master Himself is the one who completes, except that the combination would be in the tally of the cities, for He would complete one city of them. Therefore it is precise to say <b>to Him</b>, for this defense is under the defense of the Blessed One."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:42:12.882324369Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}